  "title": "U.S.-Canada Trade War Escalates with New Tariffs",
  "summary": "The U.S. president delays new tariffs on Canada for three days, aiming to finalize a deal to avoid economic strain, while Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney says Canada will match new U.S. tariffs dollar for dollar, starting September 8. Canada's levies - as high as 50% - will apply to nearly $20bn of US products, from steel to T-shirts.",
